  "id": "pr-262",
  "instruction": "Update the glom command-line interface so users can apply a glom transformation or specification to target data supplied as a command-line value, a file, or standard input. Target input must be recognized and loaded as JSON, YAML, TOML, or Python data according to the CLI’s existing argument and file conventions, including correct handling of YAML targets in the main command path. The resulting transformed value must be emitted in the CLI’s established output format, and the same behavior must work when input arrives through a pipe. Parsing must be safe: data supplied by users, especially YAML and Python-formatted input, must not be able to execute arbitrary code. Invalid formats, unreadable files, malformed data, missing required arguments, and invalid transformations/specifications must produce a clear command-line error and nonzero exit status rather than a traceback or silent result. Preserve existing CLI behavior where unrelated, and ensure the complete test and tox configuration runs successfully on Python 3.10.",
